    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLyTYAM8AAAABJ5gOdQ",
      "title": "security: point new FMAs to the Notion FMAs table",
      "author": "mds1",
      "number": 395,
      "body": "New FMAs now go in the internal [Notion FMAs table](https://www.notion.so/oplabs/Failure-Mode-Analyses-FMAs-1fb9f65a13e542e5b48af6c850763494) instead of `design-docs` / `design-docs-private`. This is the minimal change: add a one-line notice to `README.md`, `assets/fma-template.md` and `security/failure-modes-analysis.md`, and point the FMA placeholder in `assets/design-doc-template.md` at the Notion table. No files move, and existing FMAs stay in the repos as references.\n\nFollows ethereum-optimism/design-docs#394. Companion PRs update `pm`, `design-docs`, `design-docs-private` and the `op-claude-marketplace` FMA skills.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/design-docs",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-21T22:31:50Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-22T08:05:37Z",
      "additions": 10,
      "deletions": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLyTYAM8AAAABJiv1aA",
      "title": "security: let FMAs go Final once action items are tracked",
      "author": "geoknee",
      "number": 394,
      "body": "Changes when an FMA can move to **Final 👍**.\n\nBefore, Security moved an FMA to Final only once every action item was complete. Now an FMA can go Final once each action item is tracked, for example in an issue or on a project board, with a recorded decision on whether it blocks launch. The tracker, not the FMA, then gates the launch on the blocking items.\n\n- **Implementing Actions** now also asks Engineering to track each item and record whether it blocks launch.\n- The Action Items placeholders gain `Tracking` and `Blocks launch` fields, and the section intro asks for both.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/design-docs",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-20T11:58:45Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-20T13:37:42Z",
      "additions": 5,
      "deletions": 5
    }
  ],
